line 1: matrix option (1 read from files, 2 generate on-the-fly, 3 read Matrix Market file)
line 2: base name for distributed (or Matrix Market) matrix files
line 3: base name for distributed (or Matrix Market) rhs files ("none" to automatically generate rhs)
line 4: problem type for on-the-fly generated matrix (Scalar or Elasticity)
line 5: number of elements in x-direction (for on-the-fly matrix generation)
line 6: number of elements in y-direction (for on-the-fly matrix generation)
line 7: number of elements in z-direction (for on-the-fly matrix generation, 0 for 2D)
line 8: number of processors for solver
line 9: message level for MKL Pardiso
line 10: number of threads for MKL Pardiso
line 11: reordering option (0 minumum degree, 2 nested dissection, 3 parallel OpenMP ND)
line 12: debug level (0 none, 1 text output, 2 text + matrix output)
line 13: add nonsymmetry to matrix (0 no, 1 yes), testing purposes only
line 14: remove some entries to introduce non-structural-symmetry (0 no, 1 yes),
         for testing only
line 15: zero some entries (0 no, 1 yes), for testing with remove some entries
line 16: number of factorizations
line 17: output element matrix
line 18: output system matrix
